    <string name="settings_features">Features</string>
    <string name="settings_notifications">Notifications on home</string>
    <string name="settings_notifications_summary">A dot next to apps with alerts, the latest one under favorites and what\'s playing.</string>
    <string name="settings_notifications_disclosure">To show dots and music, Velora needs to read your notifications. They\'re kept only in memory while the home screen runs: never saved and never leave the phone. Private notifications are only counted, not shown.\n\nOn the next screen, turn on Velora.</string>
    <string name="settings_notifications_access">Tap to give Velora access in system settings.</string>
    <string name="settings_double_tap_lock">Double tap to lock</string>
    <string name="settings_double_tap_lock_summary">Double-tap an empty spot on home to turn the screen off.</string>
    <string name="settings_double_tap_lock_disclosure">Android only allows locking the screen from an accessibility service. Velora\'s does only that: it doesn\'t read the screen, what you type or your data.\n\nOn the next screen, find Velora and turn it on. Some phones switch it off by themselves; if that happens, Velora will tell you.</string>
